                                Lancashire. Parish church</orgName>
                            <p>Mass for Saints Egwin, Wulfstan, Oswald, Odulph, and Credan,
                                    <q>quorum reliquie in nostra requiescunt ecclesie</q>, added on
                                sig. i8v. Letter to the curate of Penwortham on sig. B6v and (in the
                                same hand) from the curates of Leylond and Penwortham on sig. A8.
                                Compare sig. A8 <q>per me <persName>Jacobum bannastr'</persName>
                                    capellanum in ecclesia penwortham.</q> Note of the xvᵐᵉ of
                                Penwortham on sig. i8.</p></provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_LaterOwners"><persName>Starkie of
                                Huntroyde</persName>: sale at Sotheby's, 29 October 1962 (£90).
                            Bookplate of <persName>Le Gendre Pierce Starkie</persName>. Compare the
                                <ref target="https://mlgb.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/book_8714"
                                >Penwortham breviary</ref>, Sotheby's 10 December 1962, lot 137 also
                            from the Starkies of Huntroyde.</provenance>
